# GitHub-standard citation metadata for THIS repository (ZenAI).
# Renders as the "Cite this repository" widget on the GitHub repo page.
#
# This repository is a published snapshot: the application code was synced from
# the development tree on 2026-05-08, and only documentation and CLI packaging
# changed after that, up to 2026-05-25. `commit` below pins the exact state, and
# `date-released` is the date that state was finalised — not the date of the
# v4.0.0 release tag (2026-03-30), which the snapshot post-dates.
#
# The memory research ZenAI builds on is a separate work with its own citation:
# see `references` at the end of this file, or cite the ZenBrain repository
# directly at https://github.com/zensation-ai/zenbrain.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ZenAI: A self-hosted AI operating system with neuroscience-inspired memory"
message: "If you use ZenAI in your research or product, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alexander
    family-names: Bering
    affiliation: "Zensation AI"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-1793-012X"
    email: "open-source@zensation.ai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zensation-ai/zenai"
url: "https://zensation.ai"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "4.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-25"
commit: "7a7ae285"
keywords:
  - "ai-operating-system"
  - "self-hosted"
  - "agent-memory"
  - "multi-agent"
  - "knowledge-graph"
  - "retrieval-augmented-generation"
  - "typescript"
abstract: >-
  ZenAI is a self-hosted AI platform that keeps persistent memory across
  sessions. It combines a multi-agent system, a knowledge graph and
  retrieval-augmented generation with the seven-layer memory architecture
  provided by ZenBrain, so that context accumulated in earlier conversations
  remains available later instead of being discarded at the end of a session.
  The platform is distributed under Apache-2.0 and is designed to run on
  infrastructure the operator controls.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "ZenBrain: A Neuroscience-Inspired 7-Layer Memory Architecture for Autonomous AI Systems"
